  "equipment_type": "Refrigerated display case controller",
  "applies_to": "PENN / Johnson Controls MR5 Series (MR534) panel-mount controllers for refrigerated display cases, with the ADPT-MR5-RS485 adapter for BACnet MS/TP or Verasys.",
  "summary": "The MR5 controls one refrigerated case: compressor, defrost, evaporator fan and alarm relays from up to three temperature sensors, with optional QREV/PSHC superheat sensor. Through the ADPT-MR5-RS485 adapter it joins a BACnet MS/TP or Verasys network and exposes 51 objects: case temperatures, relay states, QREV/PSHC readings, binary inputs, the setpoint and differential, defrost settings and defrost times, and leak/door/QREV alarms.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 1,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Time objects are printed as TV (Time Value) and shown here as type Other with the same instance.",
    "The bulletin is marked Discontinued.",
    "Sensor 1 : Temperature (AI 10005) is the only object that supports trending (144 samples, every 10 min or on COV).",
    "The table also marks which objects support BACnet alarms (sensor temperatures and the four alarm BIs).",
    "Units for temperatures follow the controller setting; the table prints ranges in °F and °C.",
    "Source: Table 29 'MR5 BACnet objects available on Verasys or standard BACnet', pages 61-64 (51 objects)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "MR5 Series Panel Mount Case Controller Technical Bulletin",
    "doc_number": "LIT-12013019",
    "revision_date": "2019-08-13",
    "url": "https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/bas/api/khub/documents/PFZ9MbhezH_qtq06OykSww/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Fit the ADPT-MR5-RS485 adapter (included on MR534AFDV), set MS/TP connectivity to BACnet and a unique device address and device ID, then read case temperature, relay states and alarms. The BMS can adjust the setpoint and differential and defrost settings.",
